SUMMARY:Lisa B’s ’60s Magic Now’ Record Release Show (Berkeley)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1634346@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Community
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSinger and spoken-word artist 
 Lisa B (Lisa Bernstein) celebrates the release or her 8th album\, “’60
 s Magic Now!: The Y-Verse\,” with her stellar band and special guests. A
 fter seven critically acclaimed records and a recent poetry book/audiobook
  with original music\, Lisa presents a collection of stunning ’60s cover
 s that are newly relevant today. Inspired by her ardent response to the re
 pressive Trump administration\, the album offers expressive new arrangemen
 ts of various beloved ’60s tunes. Their more innocent calls for love and
  peace are infused with cutting-edge flavors — straightahead jazz\, soul
 \, funk\, jazz-rock\, hip-hop\, and Latin. And Lisa’s new poetic raps re
 veal previously hidden rooms within many of the songs. The record spotligh
 ts four magical characters\, each distinct figures of freedom: Spooky\, Mr
 . Fantasy\, Ruby Tuesday\, and Windy. It includes two anthems from the tim
 e that passionately address social action: “The Times They Are A-Changin
 '” (Bob Dylan) and “Everybody Get Together” (the Youngbloods). Round
 ing out the evening are other songs from the ’60s or reminiscent of the 
 decade from Lisa’s previous records:”What’s New\, Pussycat?\,” “
 Our House\,” “What Is This Thing Called Love?\,” “With Him and Max
  Roach’s Solo\,” and various originals. Lisa B – sung and spoken voc
 als Ben Flint – keyboards Fred Randolph – bass Shawn Myers – drums a
 nd special guests! Tickets are $25 in advance and $30 at the door. Childre
 n under 12 are free. Advance t...\n\n$25.00\n\nTickets: https://www.eventv
 esta.com/events/160685-lisa-b-lisa-bernstein-s-record-release-show-60s-mag
 ic-now-the-y-verse\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lisa-bs-60s-magic-now
 -record-release-show-berkeley/\nSource: Funcheap SF
