DESCRIPTION:- Class Time: 3:00PM - 6:00PM\n\nKeeping your wardrobe in good
  shape starts with learning a few basic repairs and alterations. Maybe you
  need to shorten a pair of pants with a new hem\, fix a seam that has spli
 t open\, or sew a button back on. In this beginner-friendly class\, you wi
 ll learn hand sewing techniques to keep your favorite clothes ready to wea
 r!\n\nLessons covered in this class include:\n\n- Hemming jeans\, stretch 
 fabrics\, and delicate sheers\n\n- Repairing seams\n\n- Sewing on buttons\
 n\n- Simple mending techniques\n\nDuring class\, you will practice using a
  selection of different fabrics. We also encourage you to bring a few item
 s of your own to work on if you like. Your instructor will guide you throu
 gh all hemming and repair techniques but will not directly mend your selec
 ted items. That's where you come in!! Each student will gain a working kno
 wledge of each hemming and repair techniques\, as well as the opportunity 
 to work on 1-2 pieces from home.\n\nPlease Note: This is a beginner-friend
 ly class that does not require prior hand or machine sewing knowledge. How
 ever\, this would not be a replacement for one of our other Sewing 101 or 
 Sewing Bootcamp classes\, which give a more complete introduction to using
  sewing machines. Also\, this class will not cover replacing / repairing z
 ippers\, as that's a whole 'nother thing!!\n\nSupplies Needed: All materia
 ls for practice are provided so you can try out several techniques on diff
 erent types of fabric. You may bring a few pieces from home t...\n\n$59.75
