BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Conversation: On Archiving Punk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639660@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerGoethe-Institut e.V. / Private
 What happens when a subculture becomes history? And who gets to preserve i
 t?\nTake a look inside the San Francisco Public Library’s Punk Archive a
 nd explore the stories\, artifacts\, and creative communities that shaped 
 San Francisco’s punk history.\n\nThe evening offers a behind-the-scenes 
 look at the archive as a growing\, community-built collection\, exploring 
 how punk materials enter the archive\, how provenance helps us understand 
 their histories\, and how archivists process\, preserve\, and make these c
 ollections accessible. The event also highlights the collaborative nature 
 of punk archiving\, including the important roles of donors and contributo
 rs\, and what it means to care for fliers\, photographs\, and other epheme
 ra from an underground cultural movement.\nThe event will feature Penelope
  Houston of the Avengers\, who started the San Francisco Punk Archive with
  the support of the San Francisco Public Library\, which holds key punk ma
 terials and ephemera\; Freya Channing\, archivist of the San Francisco Pun
 k Archive and manager of the Little Maga/Zine Collection\; and Christina M
 oretta\, photo curator and manager of the San Francisco History Center at 
 the San Francisco Public Library\, the official archives for the City and 
 County of San Francisco.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.goethe.de/ins/us/
 en/sta/sfr/ver.cfm?event_id=27357571\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/con
 versation-archiving-punk/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Websit
 e-quer1.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Goethe-Institut San Francisco\, 657 Howard Street San Francisco\,
  CA 94105
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/conversation-archiving-punk/
END:VEVENT
