DESCRIPTION:Melissa LaiLawton Alternative School’s Fall Fest is bringing
  a burst of creativity to the Sunset\, and it’s free to attend. On Satur
 day\, October 10\, 2026\, families can enjoy an afternoon of community fun
  featuring local food vendors\, plus a one‑of‑a‑kind arcade inspired
  by Caine’s Arcade. Every carnival-style game has been imagined and hand
 -built by Lawton’s 5th graders using recycled and repurposed materials 
 — turning cardboard\, tape\, and everyday items into something truly mag
 ical.\nVisitors can play the student‑made games\, meet the young creator
 s behind them\, and experience a project that celebrates imagination\, tea
 mwork\, and creativity. Admission is free\, and game play and food are ava
 ilable for purchase\, with proceeds supporting the 5th graders’ graduati
 on festivities.\nIf you’re looking for a feel‑good\, family‑friendly
  event that showcases kids building something extraordinary for their comm
 unity\, Fall Fest is a perfect weekend pick.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://w
 ww.eventbrite.com/e/lawton-fall-fest-studentbuilt-arcade-community-fun-tic
 kets-2000866480505?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/law
