BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alcatraz’s Sunrise Gathering for Indigenous Peoples’ Day (2026
 )
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T041500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T080000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-382389@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous Peoples’ Day Sunrise Gathering at Alcatraz (2026)
 \nAlison Taggart-Barone via NPS\n\nThe Indigenous Peoples’ Day Sunrise G
 athering on October 12 and November 26\, 2026 are organized by the Interna
 tional Indian Treaty Council commemorating the 1969-71 occupation of Alcat
 raz by the Indians of All Tribes.\nThese are one-day events and not the st
 andard Alcatraz Island tour\; all areas except where the ceremony takes pl
 ace will be closed and inaccessible to the public.\nThe event is technical
 ly free\, but requires a $12 round trip boat trip to the island (kids 5 an
 d under are free)\n\nIncludes\n\nCommemoration of the 1969-71 occupation o
 f Alcatraz by the Indians of All Tribes\n\nSchedule\n\nOctober 12\, 2026: 
 Indigenous People’s Day\nDeparture Times: 4:15 am\, 4:30 am\, 5:00 am\, 
 5:15 am\nNovember 26\, 2026: Thanksgiving\n\nDeparture Times: 4:15 am\, 4:
 30 am\, 4:45 am\, 5:00 am\, 5:15 am\, 5:30 am\, 5:45am\, 6:00 am\n\nDress 
 Code\n\nThe weather on Alcatraz is unpredictable and subject to change une
 xpectedly\, so be sure to dress in layers…bring along a light jacket or 
 sweater\, no matter how nice the day begins! Follow this link for more inf
 ormation.\n\nWhere to Meet\n\nPier 33 Alcatraz Landing\nPier 33 Alcatraz L
 anding is the launch site to Alcatraz Island.\nAlcatraz Landing includes t
 he Ticketbooth and waiting and boarding areas\, all of which are accessibl
 e. Accessible bathrooms are found at Pier 33 Alcatraz Landing and on all A
 lcatraz Cruises vessels.\nPlease note: there are no wheelchairs available 
 for loan eit...\n\n$12.00\n\nTickets: https://alcatrazcitycruises.com/tick
 ets/sunrise-gathering-ceremony\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sunrise-g
 athering-alcatraz-indigenous-peoples-day/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/120326
 97_10153718938301554_6215023982069084485_o1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Alcatraz Island\, San Francisco\, CA 94133
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sunrise-gathering-alcatraz-indigenous-peoples-
 day/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:San Francisco Indigenous Peoples Day with special performance by J
 eremy Dutcher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T160000
DTSTAMP:20261006T002614Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-0eec3c1b7de41ae3@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:arts,festival,music
DESCRIPTION:Free RSVP\nJoin us in celebration of San Francisco Indigenous 
 Peoples Day with a magnificent profusion of Native American art\, music an
 d vendors. The event highlights the vastly diverse and talented community 
 of Indigenous artists in the Bay Area\, California and the Americas. Prese
 nted on Yelamu\, Ramaytush Ohlone Territory\, in partnership with the Inte
 rnational Indian Treaty Council\, the program at Yerba Buena Gardens follo
 ws the Annual Indigenous Peoples Day Sunrise Gathering on Alcatraz – ple
 ase check the IITC website for updates. Schedule to be announced.\n\nA gro
 undbreaking Indigenous musician whose art flows directly out of his cultur
 al activism\, tenor Jeremy Dutcher is a conservatory-trained Canadian comp
 oser\, musicologist and performer who has turned European classical music 
 into a vehicle for language preservation. A member of Neqotkuk First Natio
 n in Eastern Canada now based in Montréal\, Québec\, Dutcher catapulted 
 to renown with his debut album Wolastoqiyik Lintuwakonawa\, which won the 
 2018 Polaris Music Prize and the Juno Award for Indigenous Music Album of 
 the Year at the Canadian equivalent of the Grammys in 2019. The project un
 earthed century-old archival recordings of his ancestors\, which he turned
  into collaborative compositions on piano. Sung entirely in Wolastoqey\, h
 is endangered mother tongue\, the album led to collaborations with artists
  such as Yo-Yo Ma and Feist. His follow-up release\, 2023’s Motewolonuwo
 k\, was also awarded the Polaris Music Prize\, making Dut...\n\nPublished 
 by ybgfestival.org\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.c
 om)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://ybgfestival.org/event/sf-indigenous-peo
 ples-day-2026/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-fra
 ncisco-ca\nSource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T002614Z
LOCATION:Great Lawn\, Yerba Buena Gardens\, Mission St. between 3rd & 4th 
 Sts.\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103\, United States
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ybgfestival.org/event/sf-indigenous-peoples-day-2026/?utm_sour
 ce=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
