CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event Organizer© privateJoin us for a lively
  conversation between author and journalist Lin Hierse and translator-scho
 lar Dr. Jon Cho-Polizzi. Hierse’s writing navigates the complexities of 
 life in contemporary Germany\, exploring links between language\, place\, 
 and belonging across generations. Her works are characterized by complex a
 mbiguities\, settings and narratives that compound and merge\, demonstrati
 ng unexpected connections and continuities. Together they will discuss Hie
 rse‘s explorations of German and Chinese entanglements in her writing\, 
 the role of Chinatowns across the diaspora\, and the publication of her wo
 rks in English translation in new and forthcoming anthologies.\nLin Hierse
 \n\nLin Hierse is a prolific author\, journalist\, poet\, and public intel
 lectual. With a background in Asian Studies and Human Geography\, she is a
  longtime contributor to several major German journals and periodicals\; s
 he wrote the biweekly column “Poetical Correctness” in taz from 2020-2
 023. Her acclaimed autofictional debut novel Wovon wir träumen [What We D
 ream Of] was published in 2022 and follows the interconnected stories of t
 hree generations of women whose lives are ruptured and reunited through th
 e experience of migration and life in the Chinese diaspora. It was followe
 d in 2024 by her sophomore novel Das Verschwinden der Welt [The Disappeari
 ng World]\, a novel that chronicles the life of an aging tenement building
  in the outskirts of Shanghai: a one-time refuge for peasa...\n\nFree\n\nT
 ickets: https://www.goethe.de/ins/us/en/sta/sfr/ver.cfm?event_id=27355384\
 nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/conversation-unwriting-place/\nSource: F
 uncheap SF
