DESCRIPTION:Filipino American International Book Festival 2026 (SF Main Li
 brary)\nPAWA – Philippine Writers and Artists\nFilBookFest 8\, the Filip
 ino American International Book Festival\, returns to the San Francisco Pu
 blic Library on October 17-18\, 2026. This free\, two-day event celebrates
  Filipino American stories during Filipino American History Month with pan
 el discussions\, book signings\, and readings by writers\, scholars\, and 
 creatives from the U.S.\, Canada\, and the Philippines.\nOriginal Event De
 scription:\n_FilBookFest returns this October 17-18 in the SF Public Libra
 ry\, celebrating Filipino American stories with panels\, signings & readin
 gs.The Filipino American International Book Festival (FilBookFest) returns
  on October for its 8th iteration\, continuing its legacy as the largest F
 ilipino American literary festival in the U.S.Held during Filipino America
 n History Month\, FilBookFest brings together an exciting array of writers
 \, scholars\, and creatives from across the globe\, including the U.S\, Ca
 nada\, and the Philippines\, to the iconic San Francisco Public Library.Fe
 stival attendees will enjoy panel discussions\, book signings\, and readin
 gs featuring a vibrant mix of established and emerging voices. This two-da
 y event is a celebration of storytelling\, culture\, and the diverse exper
 iences of the Filipino diaspora._\nText extracted from provided image:\nSA
 NGGALAN\nSTORIES THAT PROPEL US\, STORIES THAT PROTECT US\nOCTOBER 17-18\,
  2026\nSan Francisco Main Library\, 100 Larkin St.\nSan Francisco Publi...
 \n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/filbookfest-8-2026-ticke
 ts-1994018927289\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/filipino-american-inter
 national-book-festival-2026-sf-main-library/\nSource: Funcheap SF
