DESCRIPTION:Discover science fun and excitement together at the Bay Area S
 cience Festival — Northern California’s largest free all-ages science 
 event. Experience 125+ mind-blowing hands-on experiments\, games\, demonst
 rations\, stage performances\, film screenings and science talks. Bring th
 e whole family to race robots\, see your own brainwaves\, participate in a
  science podcast\, marvel at science magic shows\, meet reptiles and amphi
 bians face-to-face and much more. Organized by UCSF\, the festival is Satu
 rday\, October 17\, 11AM-4PM at UCSF’s Mission Bay Campus amid Koret Qua
 d’s expansive lawns\, walkways\, pine grove and renowned educational\, m
 edical and biotech research facilities — one block from Chase Center. Le
 arn more at www.BayAreaScienceFestival.org.\n\nFree\n\nDetails: https://do
 thebay.com/events/2026/10/17/bay-area-science-festival-tickets\nSource: Do
