DESCRIPTION:Inventurous\nTransform everyday film plastics into durable\, l
 eather-like sheets using heat and pressure. Learn how to fuse materials su
 ch as newspaper delivery bags and soft plastic packaging into reusable tex
 tiles that can be cut\, sewn\, and shaped like fabric. Tara de la Garza of
  Inventurous demonstrates the process and shares creative ways to repurpos
 e plastic waste into functional projects.\nInventurous is a community-base
 d organization that transforms locally sourced plastic waste into useful\,
  high-value products. By engaging community members in collecting\, sortin
 g\, and processing discarded plastics\, Inventurous demonstrates practical
  approaches to reducing waste through creative reuse.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: 
 https://sfpl.org/events/2026/10/18/workshop-reduce-plastic-waste-through-c
 reative-reuse\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/reduce-plastic-waste-creat
 ive-reuse-sf-main-library/\nSource: Funcheap SF
