BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Presentation: Eyewitness to the Resistance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17914032@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Activism
DESCRIPTION:Indivisible SF presents a panel of local photojournalists from
  Pro Bono Photo and other news organizations who share selections from the
 ir portfolios and discuss the role photojournalism plays in documenting pr
 otest\, civic action and pro-democracy movements.\n\nFrom the civil rights
  and voting rights movements of the 1960s to today's social justice action
 s\, the San Francisco Bay Area has long been a significant site of protest
  and civil disobedience. Who documents these fleeting moments of protest a
 nd civic action? Local photojournalists share their experiences covering p
 ro-democracy movements and street demonstrations throughout the Bay Area.\
 n\nHear firsthand accounts from photographers documenting recent protests 
 and demonstrations\, view a curated projection of their work and engage di
 rectly with the panelists during an audience Q&A.\n\nPop-Up Gallery: A sel
 ection of photographs by participating photojournalists will be displayed 
 alongside historical protest photography from SFPL collections\, connectin
 g contemporary documentation of Bay Area demonstrations with the Library's
  photographic record of protest and civic action. The display will be on v
 iew on the 4th Floor of the Main Library from Sept. 17-Dec. 31.\n\nFree\n\
 nPresented by San Francisco Public Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public L
 ibrary\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl.org/Eyewitness-Resistance\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/presentation-eyewitness-to-the-resista
 nce-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.co
 m/free-panel-bay-area-protest-photojournalists-popup-exhibit-sf-main-libra
 ry/\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/macabre-marvels-stack-inspiration-sf-librar
 ys-hidden-books/
