BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One City One Book: Cities as Ancestors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17914044@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Explore how our relationships with cities\, parks and the more
 -than-human world can shape our future. Inspired by Susanna Kwan's Awake i
 n the Floating City\, the 2026 One City One Book selection\, this conversa
 tion brings together local community leaders working on place-based enviro
 nmental justice to consider what it means to be an ancestor and how the pl
 aces we inhabit become part of our collective legacy.\n\nDrawing on five y
 ears of the Parks as Ancestors series\, inspired by the book\, What Kind o
 f Ancestor Do You Want to Be?\, the discussion expands the conversation be
 yond protected parklands to consider urban spaces as living legacies.\n\nT
 his interactive program invites participants to consider what we inherit f
 rom the places and people who came before us-and what we will leave behind
  for those who come after. Attendees are welcome to bring a photograph or 
 a sentimental object honoring someone they have lost\, if they wish to inc
 orporate it into the program.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by San Francisco Public
  Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public Library\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl
 .org/OCOB-Panel\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/27/one-city-
 one-book-cities-as-ancestors-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34760574/859caa5b-3764-4937-bce5-ac66dee0ce67.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Koret Auditorium (SF Public Library)\, 100 Larkin St\, San Franci
 sco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/27/one-city-one-book-cities-as-anc
 estors-tickets
END:VEVENT
