CATEGORIES:Shopping
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 31\, 2026\, 11:00 am - 11:45 am\n\nStop by 
 the Foodwise Classroom for a cooking demo featuring the seasonal bounty of
  the Ferry Plaza Farmers Market.\n\nDuring the height of the pandemic\, So
 fía Jiménez began offering free meals to her community\, an effort that
  was just as rewarding as it was costly. She hoped to start her own nonpro
 fit\, hire a crew\, and distribute more meals\, which led her to make her 
 first batch of guava-filled coyotas (a style of pastry from Sonora\, Mexic
 o) as a fundraiser. Using her grandmothers recipes\, she sold coyotas to h
 er immediate family and friends\, and then to her larger community. Sofí
 a then worked with the nonprofit Mandela Partners to launch Tutuli Mexican
  Bakery and gain access to more sales opportunities in local farmers marke
 ts\, including the Ferry Plaza Farmers Market. You can find Tutuli at the 
 Ferry Plaza Farmers Market on Saturdays.\n\nAll demos take place in the Fo
 odwise Classroom (green tent in front of the Ferry Building) and are free 
 to the public\, with recipes and samples for all.\n\nTickets: https://food
 wise.org/events/sofia-jimenez-tutuli-mexican-bakery/\nDetails: https://dot
 hebay.com/events/2026/10/31/sofia-jimenez-tutuli-mexican-bakery-tickets\nS
 ource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/sf-cake-picn
 ic-fall-2026-taste-100s-cakes-halloween-levis-plaza/
