SUMMARY:Dance Heals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17882154@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:As part of the ongoing Raising Voices series\, Dance Heals gat
 hers eight films that meet some of life’s hardest realities and answer t
 hem with movement. Ukrainian women wield choreography as testimony. A flam
 enco master performs in clothing historically reserved for women. A double
  amputee becomes a withered tree blooming anew. Each piece is less about t
 he wound than what grows from it\, blending poetry\, cinematography\, and 
 activism in service of repair.\n\nCo-curated by laura elaine ellis and fol
 lowed by a panel discussion\, the screening is presented at Catharine Clar
 k Gallery alongside a concurrent exhibition by Los Angeles-based artist Sa
 ndow Birk\, whose work confronting history\, justice\, and war offers a co
 mpelling companion lens for these stories. A live performance by dazaun.da
 nce\, featuring Dazaun Soleyn\, Jordon E. Dabney\, and Claire Fisher-Mende
 z in their "work may we heal?" will precede the films.\n\nCome witness wha
 t movement can hold\, and what it can mend.\n\n25-45\n2026 SF Dance Film F
 estival:\n\nTickets: https://sfdancefilmfest.org/fall-festival-2026/dance-
 heals/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/4/dance-heals-tickets
 \nSource: DoTheBay
