BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marjorie Keller: Intimate Observer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17900140@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 6:30pm / Film 7pm\n\n$15 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nMarjorie Keller was one of the most significant figure
 s in late 20th century American experimental film. A profoundly original a
 rtist\, scholar\, teacher and advocate\, Keller was staunchly feminist wit
 hout limiting herself to that movement’s ideological orthodoxies. Fierce
 ly independent\, her work was sharply critical of the customary role women
  were relegated to in patriarchal society\, even as she embraced aspects o
 f traditional family life. Keller cherished the mostly male history of ava
 nt-garde filmmaking\, but she was one of the foremost advocates for women 
 film artists throughout her life. When she died at age 43 in 1994\, Keller
  had already produced twenty-seven 8mm and 16mm films. They were remarkabl
 e for their thematic and poetical complexity and by investigating her dome
 stic life as a woman for their starting point. Her expressive cinematograp
 hy and intricate montage were sensual\, emotional and intellectually chall
 enging\, and while she was clearly influenced by such predecessors as Mari
 e Menken\, Stan Brakhage and Saul Levine\, Keller's cinematic voice was di
 stinctly her own from beginning with her first film.\n\nIn conjunction wit
 h the publication of a new book on Keller's work\, In the Absence of Marjo
 rie Keller\, edited by Robin Blaetz and Scott Hammen\, two programs of her
  films\, spanning twenty-four years\, will be presented by Berkeley Art Mu
 seum and Pacific Film Archive and San Francisco Cinematheq...\n\n$15\n\nTi
 ckets: https://link.dice.fm/c6efa9376c13\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/ev
 ents/2026/11/5/marjorie-keller-intimate-observer-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34695674/4faae3df-e20b-4097-ac2b-13878c1a4f8f.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/marjorie-keller-intimate-observe
 r-tickets
END:VEVENT
