BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:La nuit au musée: A Sip of the Roaring 20's - 6pm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T223000
DTSTAMP:20261006T002614Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-8d1de591dec2f7ca@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:arts,drink,festival,music
DESCRIPTION:6pm-11pm | Thursday\, November 51345 Bush Street\, San Francis
 co\, CA 94109For one night\, the Francophone Museum of San Francisco trans
 forms into a 1920s speakeasy. Step back into les années folles and into a
 n evening of live music\, dancing\, and Jazz Age glamour.When Prohibition 
 threatened to dry out California\, French winemakers and traditions helped
  keep the state's wine alive\, one more thread tying France and California
  together. Tonight we explore that history\, with Prohibition-era cocktail
 s and wines to sip and a Francophone buffet to savor.Come dressed in your 
 finest flapper party attire for a night of casino games\, a short talk on 
 Prohibition in the Bay Area from historian Rebecca Yerger\, and two live s
 ets of jazz from Charles Unger Experience and La Gauloise All Stars. Our C
 harleston swing lesson will have you out on the dance floor in no time.Tic
 kets: $60 general\, $50 for AFSF members\, in advance only. $80 at the doo
 r. Ticket holders will receive a secret password and instructions for entr
 y.Grab your ticket\, don your flapper best\, and we'll see you on the othe
 r side of the door.\n\nPublished by Alliance Française de San Francisco -
  Public Calendar\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com
 )\, ODbL 1.0\n\nSource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T002614Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
