SUMMARY:29th Anniversary San Francisco Transgender Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T002614Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-790aadbd37a2ddb1@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:festival,film
DESCRIPTION:The San Francisco Transgender Film Festival (SFTFF) celebrates
  29 years of innovative\, experimental\, and outside-the-box films by tran
 sgender and gender-nonconforming filmmakers.\n\n​​Spanning 12-days fro
 m November 12-22 and comprised of seven short film programs showcasing 37 
 films\, SFTFF 2026 will be a hybrid festival\, presented both in person an
 d online\, and featuring a range of genres from documentaries and politics
  to animation\, dance\, music\, romance\, coming-of-age tales\, and thrill
 ers.\n\nSFTFF will host in-person programs Nov. 12-14 at the Roxie Theater
 \, 3117 16th St.\, SF and will offer on demand access to each of the progr
 ams through Nov. 22nd. Films are closed captioned for Deaf and hard-of-hea
 ring audiences\; tickets are $0-$50\, sliding scale/donation-based\, inclu
 sive of fees.\nhttps://www.indybay.org/newsitems/2026/08/24/18888179.php\n
 \nPublished by Indybay\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscove
 ry.com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://www.indybay.org/newsitems/2026/08/2
 4/18888179.php?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-fra
 ncisco-ca\nSource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T002614Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater 3117 16th St\, San Francisco\, CA 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.indybay.org/newsitems/2026/08/24/18888179.php?utm_source=c
 aldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca
