BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dorian Wood: Canto de Todes + Roco Córdova
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17663884@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 7:30pm / Show 8pm\n\n$29 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nMember tickets are not yet available for Fall 2026 Pro
 grams\n\nWeaving together chamber classical\, folk\, torch song\, and expe
 rimental music\, Dorian Wood’s Canto de Todes is a 70-minute distillatio
 n born from Wood’s acclaimed 12-hour composition and installation. The t
 itle—Spanish for “Song of Everyone”—is inspired by a lyric of the 
 late Chilean singer and songwriter Violeta Parra. Canto de Todes emphasize
 s the urgency of music as a vessel for social change\, and honors the ance
 stral trajectory of Wood’s Costa Rican-Nicaraguan family and their exper
 ience in the U.S.\n\nDorian Wood (b. 1975\, pronouns: she/her/they/them) i
 s an anti-disciplinary artist based in the U.S.\, whose practice seeks to 
 “infect” spaces and ideologies in order to challenge traditions and sy
 stems of marginalization. Her performances\, films and visual works have b
 een presented worldwide. From 2019–2020\, Wood toured internationally wi
 th XAVELA LUX AETERNA\, a chamber orchestra tribute to Chavela Vargas. Sub
 sequent works Mares Ocultos (2022)\, a compositional series centering on d
 econstructing male heterosexuality.\n\nBorn in San Juan\, Puerto Rico\, Ro
 co Córdova is a vocalist\, composer\, producer and improviser based in th
 e San Francisco Bay Area. They possess a B.Mus. in Composition from the Pu
 erto Rico Conservatory of Music and an M.A. in Composition from Mills Coll
 ege in Oakland\, California. They have studied under the guidance of Carlo
 s Carri...\n\n$29\n\nTickets: https://link.dice.fm/Ibd4d3e150c5\nDetails: 
 https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/dorian-wood-canto-de-todes-roco-cor
 dova-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33577742/200c6931-e022-44e0-8a37-450f0f2642d6.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/13/dorian-wood-canto-de-todes-roco
 -cordova-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Max Jaffe: You Want That Too! + Burden of Dreams
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T103000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17845411@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 8pm / Show 8:30pm\n\n$23 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nIn a trio formation with some of the core rhythm secti
 on players from the record\, Max Jaffe\, Gavin Gamboa\, and Logan Kane rei
 magine the music from Jaffe's 2025 release You Want That Too!\n\nMax Jaffe
  is a drummer\, producer\, composer\, and technologist based in Los Angele
 s\, CA. His work expands the possibilities of composition and collaboratio
 n through the drum set.\n\nIn 2025\, Jaffe released "You Want That Too!" o
 n Colorfield Records. Eclectic and tuneful\, the album received praise fro
 m Pitchfork and is being followed with a series of special live performanc
 es in varying formations.\n\nMax is a founding member of experimental rock
  collective JOBS\, Amirtha Kidambi's Elder Ones\, and several others. He h
 as toured\, performed\, and recorded with many diverse artists including W
 ild Up\, Steph Richards\, Nels Cline\, Ava Mendoza\, Cass McCombs\, DARKSI
 DE\, Normal Love\, Jeff Parker\, Vinny Golia\, Peter Evans\, and many othe
 rs.\n\nBurden of Dreams is the latest band from Oakland composer and multi
 -instrumentalist\, Nathan Clevenger. Along with Clevenger on electric bass
 \, the ensemble features Brett Carson (Hammond organ)\, Mark Pascucci-Clif
 ford (vibraphone)\, and Jason Levis (drums). The band's music is dark and 
 dense\, drawing from 20th Century classical\, doom rock\, and jazz.\n\nPho
 to by Alex De La Hidalga.\n\n$23\n\nTickets: https://link.dice.fm/a5174866
 35f7\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/max-jaffe-you-want-t
 hat-too-burden-of-dreams-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
