BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ann M. Evans and Georgeanne Brennan\, Market Memories Cookbook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T130000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17747609@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Shopping
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\, 11:00 am - 11:45 am\n\nStop by
  the Foodwise Classroom for a cooking demo featuring the seasonal bounty o
 f the Ferry Plaza Farmers Market.\n\nGeorgeanne Brennan is a James Beard a
 nd Julia Child award-winning cookbook author. Her association with farmers
  markets goes back to the 1980s\, when her pioneering seed company\, Le Ma
 rche Seeds\, supplied emerging market growers across the country. Her memo
 ir\, A Pig in Provence\, chronicles her adventures in France\, where she s
 till has a home\, raising pigs and making goats milk cheese. She lives in 
 Winters\, California\, with her husband.\n\nAnn M. Evans is a co-founder o
 f the Davis Farmers Market and the Davis Food Co-op\, and she is a former 
 mayor of Davis\, California. A leading proponent of the Farm-to-School mov
 ement in California\, she worked extensively with former California School
  Superintendent Delaine Eastin and with Alice Waters on multiple projects.
  She writes a weekly column for the Davis Enterprise. This is her third co
 okbook. She lives with her husband in Davis.\n\nThey are the co-authors of
  Market Memories Cookbook: Celebrating 50 Years.\n\nAll demos take place i
 n the Foodwise Classroom (green tent in front of the Ferry Building) and a
 re free to the public\, with recipes and samples for all.\n\nThe demo will
  be followed by a book signing with book sales courtesy of Book Passage.\n
 \nTickets: https://foodwise.org/events/ann-m-evans-and-georgeanne-brennan-
 market-memories-cookbook/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21
 /ann-m-evans-and-georgeanne-brennan-market-memories-cookbook-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay
