BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alcatraz’s Thanksgiving Indigenous Peoples’ Sunrise Ceremony (
 2026)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T041500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261126T080000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1234124@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous Peoples’ Day Sunrise Gathering at Alcatraz (2026)
 \nAlison Taggart-Barone via NPS\n\nThe Indigenous Peoples’ Day Sunrise G
 athering on October 12 and November 26\, 2026 are organized by the Interna
 tional Indian Treaty Council commemorating the 1969-71 occupation of Alcat
 raz by the Indians of All Tribes.\nThese are one-day events and not the st
 andard Alcatraz Island tour\; all areas except where the ceremony takes pl
 ace will be closed and inaccessible to the public.\nThe event is technical
 ly free\, but requires a $12 round trip boat trip to the island (kids 5 an
 d under are free)\n\nIncludes\n\nCommemoration of the 1969-71 occupation o
 f Alcatraz by the Indians of All Tribes\n\nSchedule\n\nOctober 12\, 2026: 
 Indigenous People’s Day\nDeparture Times: 4:15 am\, 4:30 am\, 5:00 am\, 
 5:15 am\nNovember 26\, 2026: Thanksgiving\n\nDeparture Times: 4:15 am\, 4:
 30 am\, 4:45 am\, 5:00 am\, 5:15 am\, 5:30 am\, 5:45am\, 6:00 am\n\nDress 
 Code\n\nThe weather on Alcatraz is unpredictable and subject to change une
 xpectedly\, so be sure to dress in layers…bring along a light jacket or 
 sweater\, no matter how nice the day begins! Follow this link for more inf
