CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 8pm / Show 8:30pm\n\n$23 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nJeremiah Chiu is a synthesist in the broadest sense of
  the word—a craftsperson of the modular synth and other musical instrume
 nts and tools\, as well as an artist\, designer\, and educator whose work 
 continually brings disparate forms of knowledge into new relationships. Wh
 ile widely recognized for his versatile electronic music as a solo artist\
 , textured recordings in a duo with violist Marta Sofia Honer\, and the ex
 perimental quintet he co-leads\, SML\, Chiu has simultaneously maintained 
 a practice as a graphic designer and visual artist\, developing a practice
  attentive to both the structure of technological systems and the continge
 ncies of liveness and emergence.\n\nFor Chiu\, visual thinking and musical
  thinking are not separate disciplines but different expressions of the sa
 me innate compositional sensibility. This point of view is born equally fr
 om his idiosyncratic sense of aesthetics and his capacity for a warm and p
 orous exchange within a thriving community of creative collaborators that 
 stretches between Chicago and Los Angeles.\n\nRooted in Chicago's deeply i
 nterconnected experimental music community\, his music has consistently de
 veloped through long-term collaborations and shared artistic inquiry. Foll
 owing years of performing with groups including Icy Demons and Chandeliers
  and within the Shape Shoppe collective\, Chiu emerged as a distinctive vo
 ice on the International Anthem label through a series...\n\n$23\n\nTicket
 s: https://link.dice.fm/Z0f00203e7e6\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events
 /2026/12/3/jeremiah-chiu-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
